Z||000003||rogergarrison||10-06-2001||05:53 PM||||he WAS medieval french. I agree most are very vague and can be made to say anything. But when he does name exact places and people by name, it does get interesting. In case you dont know his story, he wrote all these predictions to intentionally be vague. He had the possiblity of being executed by not doing so. A couple of specificly named items:<BR>He stated that the queen of France would be abducted in Verrone France, and that she would be beheaded. Happened where and to who he said. Even described her clothing.<P>He named Alba as the island the 1st anti-christ would be exiled to and come to power  and he would be from France. Fits exactly Napoleon.<P>He named the 2nd anti-christ as coming from the area of the Danube, and would be a great public speaker and would lead his nation to try to take over the continent. He said his name would be Hister. Very similar to Hitler, who did come from the Danube River area of Germany.<P>He also stated war would be made by men in machines in the air and under the sea. (planes and submarines) <P>He states that mankind would set foot on luna. We, at least supposedly, did put men on the moon.<P>Those were some of his statements that I wouldnt say are very vague but pretty accurate. There are dozens and dozens of more like those. Ive also read several books on him that say much more than you see in the tv documentaries. You have to realize he wrote all these hundreds of years ago. Modern so called prophets tell you what they said about events after the fact. His have been written for hundreds of years ahead. You have to also realize that he wrote about things that no one in that era would have no comprehension of. For example, no one had a submarine before the mid 19th century. I just keep an open mind myself. He does seem to say an awful lot of coincidences.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||10-06-2001||05:57 PM||||In fact, he went into a "trance" when he wrote the quatrains - which means he was getting high on some kind of drug.<P>His quatrains are an interesting read, but given enough time <B>all</B> predictions will come true.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||California Kid||10-06-2001||07:20 PM||||The TV Special was pretty entertaining, makes you think and wonder. The main thing that always bugs me is the way they portray the time table of his predictions. Did they translate right, is he that accurate, or did they bend the lines a little to fit the timeframe??? Not being an astrologer, I don't have a clue.<P>Kind of agree with Cliff, if you can think of it, sooner or later it's going to happen!!<P>On the humorous side, this photo should be captioned "When I finish this, I'm going to write down some predictions!!!"<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Predictions.jpg"> ||||reg||1
